# R14 — what does NOT leave this machine on an EAS build.
#
# SECURITY-LESSONS.md R14 records Talise's Critical C2: production database dumps and
# Apple signing keys were uploaded to a third-party build service on every mobile build.
# EAS uploads the project directory as a tarball, so this file is the control that keeps
# that from happening again. It is enforced BEFORE the first build, not after.
#
# .gitignore is NOT consulted when .easignore exists, so everything that must stay
# local is restated here in full. See README.md § "What leaves this machine".

# ── secrets: never, under any circumstance ──────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# ── anything resembling data ────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sql
*.dump
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
/fixtures/
/dumps/

# ── local artefacts with no business in a build ─────────────────────────────
.screenshots/
.expo/
dist/
coverage/
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store

# ── repo material the app build does not need ───────────────────────────────
/test/
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
vitest.config.ts
